{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC3 DECISION RECORDED — the WRITER is NOT changed; the fix is reader-side tolerance only.\n\nDecision: `_store/event_append._prepare_event` keeps creating the ticket directory BEFORE its\nfirst event (`os.makedirs(ticket_dir, exist_ok=True)`), and the plan-relation reducer tolerates\nthe resulting event-less directory instead. The reasoning is recorded as a code comment at that\nexact makedirs site so it is not re-litigated.\n\nReasoning, three independent reasons:\n\n1. A writer-side cleanup CANNOT cover the observed failure mode. The write path is makedirs ->\n   stage temp -> under-lock atomic rename. The orphans we found came from PROCESS DEATH\n   (crash/kill/timeout) inside that window; a best-effort rmdir on the staging-failure path only\n   closes the narrow subset that already raises a Python exception, and leaves the actual\n   mechanism intact.\n2. Cleanup is UNSAFE under this store's concurrency model. Many sessions write one shared\n   .tickets-tracker. Removing a directory another session just created races its in-flight write.\n   This is the same 'tolerate, never tidy' rule already established for stray .tmp-event-* files\n   (see test_resign_tolerates_a_concurrent_writer_churning_tracker_temp_files).\n3. Only the reader-side fix REPAIRS EXISTING BROKEN CLONES. A writer change does nothing for a\n   clone already carrying an orphan — and since git cannot track empty directories, such a clone\n   cannot be repaired by pulling either.\n\nScope of the tolerance is deliberately NARROW and mutation-proven in both directions:\n* event-less directory -> skipped with a WARNING naming the absolute path (RED before the fix\n  reproduced the exact reported signature: reason=reducer-error reference=0de5-6db1-8058-4e80).\n* directory that DOES hold events but still fails to reduce -> still raises reducer-error, so a\n  genuinely corrupt ticket that may carry relation material never gets silently dropped. Proven\n  by mutating _holds_no_events to `return True`: the narrowness test then FAILS with\n  'DID NOT RAISE PlanRelationSnapshotError'.\n\nCommit: a30dc6c22b (branch fix/043f-84aa-infra; NOT pushed to Gerrit per instruction)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785727387624469001,"uuid":"39795cb5-569a-4cf9-8a7f-621e0b43e436"}